msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This screen shows your character's set of talents. You can gain new abilities via certain items, through religion or by way of mutations. Activation of an ability usually comes at a cost, e.g. Magic power. Press '<w>!</w>' or '<w>?</w>' to toggle between ability selection and description."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This screen shows the skill set of your character. The number next to the skill is your current level, the higher the better. <w>Training</w> displays training percentages. <w>Costs</w> displays relative training costs. <w>Targets</w> displays skill training targets. You can toggle which skills to train by pressing their slot letters. A <darkgrey>grey</darkgrey> skill will not be trained and ease the training of others."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "The training percentage (in <brown>brown</brown>) shows the relative amount of the experience gained which will be used to train each skill. It is automatically set depending on which skills you have used recently. Disabling a skill sets the training rate to 0."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "The training cost (in <cyan>cyan</cyan>) shows the experience cost to raise the given skill one level, relative to the cost of raising an aptitude zero skill from level zero to level one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Press the letter of a skill to set a training target. When the target is reached a message will appear and the training of the skill will be disabled."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This screen shows the skill set of your character. Press the letter of a skill to read its description, or press <w>?</w> again to return to the skill selection."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This screen shows the spells in your spell library. From here you can memorise spells by selecting them, as well as view spell descriptions, search for them, and organize them. As a conjurer, you start with five memorisable spells, and one already memorised: Magic Dart. (To view memorised spells, you can exit this menu and select <w>I</w>.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"\n"
"A spell that isn't <darkgray>grayed out</darkgray> or <lightred>forbidden</lightred> can be memorised right away by selecting it at this menu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "When wielded, some weapons (such as this one) offer certain abilities you can activate. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "You can wield this weapon with <w>%</w>, or use <w>%</w> to switch between the weapons in slot a and b. (Use <w>%i</w> to adjust item slots.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "To attack a monster, you can simply walk into it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Because of your horns you cannot wear helmets. (Press <w>%</w> to see a list of your mutations and innate abilities.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Only nagas and armataurs can wear barding."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"Note that body armour with a high encumbrance rating may hinder your ability to cast spells. Light armour such as robes and leather armour will be generally safe for any aspiring spellcaster."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"Note that shields will hinder your ability to cast spells, until you've gained enough Shields skill to remove the penalty."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"Note that many ranged weapons are two handed and so cannot be used with an offhand item."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "The magic within can be unleashed by evoking (<w>%</w>) it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "A manual can greatly help you in training a skill. After you pick one up, the skill in question will be trained more efficiently and will level up faster until you exhaust the manual's contents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can pick up a spellbook to add its spells to your spell library. (View your spell library with <w>%</w>.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Skeletons and corpses can be used as components for certain necromantic spells. Apart from that, they are largely useless."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This staff can enhance your spellcasting, making spells of its related spell school more powerful."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Miscellaneous items sometimes harbour magical powers that can be harnessed by e<w>%</w>oking the item."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "These nasty constructions can cause a range of unpleasant effects. You won't be able to avoid tripping traps by flying over them; their magic construction will cause them to be triggered anyway."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"The dungeon contains a number of natural obstacles such as shafts, which lead one to three levels down. Once you know the shaft is there, you can safely step over it.\n"
"If you want to jump down there, use <w>></w> to do so. Be warned that getting back here might be difficult."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Some areas of the dungeon, such as the Spider Nest, may be strewn with giant webs that may ensnare you for a short time. Insects, oozes and incorporeal entities can navigate the webs safely."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "You can enter the next (deeper) level by following them down (<w>></w>). To get back to this level again, press <w><<</w> while standing on the upstairs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid " In Tiles, you can achieve the same, in either direction, by clicking the <w>left mouse button</w>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"\n"
"You have not yet passed through this particular set of stairs. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "These stairs lead out of the dungeon. Following them will end the game. The only way to win is to transport the fabled Orb of Zot outside."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "You can enter the previous (shallower) level by following these up (<w><<</w>). This is ideal for retreating or finding a safe resting spot, since the previous level will have less monsters, and monsters on this level can't follow you up unless they're standing right next to you. To get back to this level again, press <w>></w> while standing on the downstairs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid " In Tiles, you can perform either action simply by clicking the <w>left mouse button</w> instead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Escape hatches can be used to quickly leave a level with <w><<</w> and <w>></w>, respectively. Note that you will usually be unable to return right away."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid ""
"\n"
"To avoid accidentally opening a door you'd rather remain closed during travel or autoexplore, you can mark it with an exclusion from the map view (<w>X</w>) with <w>ee</w> while your cursor is on the grid in question. Such an exclusion will prevent autotravel from ever entering that grid until you remove the exclusion with another press of <w>Xe</w>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This is your chance to join a religion! In general, the gods will help their followers, bestowing powers of all sorts upon them, but many of them demand a life of dedication, constant tributes or entertainment in return.\n"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "This particular altar is so ancient that you cannot make out which god it is dedicated to! Converting here by pressing <w>></w> while standing on the altar will enter you into service of a random god, who will grant you some additional piety in thanks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "An entryway into one of the many dungeon side branches in Crawl. "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "h.hints"
msgid "Beware, sometimes these can be deadly!"
msgstr ""

